---
// -- SEO COPY REWRITE APPLIED, 16 September 2026 -------------------------
//
// This page has been rewritten against carpet-and-rug-cleaning-copy-rewrite.md
// (workbook row 7, primary `carpet cleaning` 4,600/mo, cluster 12,250/mo, the
// largest in the workbook). Section numbers in the comments below are that
// brief's, and it SUPERSEDES the "NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS" note below.
//
// THE ROOT-CAUSE FINDING, and most of what changed: the mapped primary is
// `carpet cleaning`, and the page was built on "carpet AND RUG cleaning".
// Those three words split the phrase in the title, the URL, the H1, the
// opening paragraph, the meta and the FAQ heading, and the scoring rules
// treat a split phrase as absent. So the page scored nothing on the exact
// term in five places while reading as though it was about exactly the right
// subject. The metadata, H1, hero lead and second FAQ heading below are the
// same fix applied five times. RUGS ARE NOT DROPPED ANYWHERE. They move a
// few words to the right.
//
// Also implemented: the approved CTA in all four places, stairs landed in the
// hero and in method stage three, a new end-of-lease H2, a new hire-machine
// FAQ, the narrowed comparison table and the full-footprint town list.
//
// NO BLOCKING CONFLICT on this page. The approved CTA, "Book your clean
// online", RESOLVES the live contradiction between the buttons and the
// pricing paragraph rather than creating one.
//
// Not done here, because they are not copy: the URL mismatch (the workbook
// wants /house-cleaning/carpet-cleaning, which is also the only one of the
// two URLs carrying the mapped phrase contiguously, so it is a redirect
// decision for the build team), the canonical domain, FAQ schema for eleven
// questions across two blocks, dropping the header's competing "Get an
// instant quote", and hiding the testimonial block until real quotes exist.
//
// Carpet and rug cleaning — one of the six "Appliances" leaf pages under the
// Home Cleaning mega-menu, all built in the same pass and sharing a
// structure. Their cluster links come from src/data/appliance-services.ts;
// read that file's header first, including the note on why "Appliances" is
// the wrong word for this group.
//
// NO CONTENT BRIEF EXISTS for any of the six. All copy is DRAFTED from the
// brand foundation document, which governs voice and claim rules but supplies
// no operational detail. Facts only TLB holds ship as visible [brackets].
//
// ⚠️ THIS PAGE HAS A COMMERCIAL TWIN. /commercial-cleaning/commercial-carpet-cleaning/ covers the
// same method for workplaces. They must stay in their lanes or they compete
// for the same queries: THAT page is offices, strata and after-hours trading;
// THIS page is a family living room, a wool rug and pets. The two link each
// other once, and neither repeats the other's argument. The Award and
// after-hours penalty-rate material belongs only to the commercial page; the
// wool and pet material belongs only to this one.
//
// BLOCKS LAUNCH:
//   - IS THIS DELIVERED IN HOUSE? Same unanswered question as the commercial
//     twin. Extraction needs a machine, and nothing in any brief says TLB
//     owns one. If it is subcontracted, the comparison table below (row one:
//     "employed by TLB, not subcontracted") contradicts the page it sits on
//     and must come off.
//   - WOOL AND NATURAL FIBRE. The page says outright that TLB tests fibre
//     first and treats wool differently. Confirm TLB is equipped and willing
//     to clean wool and natural-fibre rugs at all. Plenty of cleaners decline
//     them and refer to a specialist rug plant, which is a perfectly good
//     answer — but it has to be the real one, because branded FAQ 3 promises
//     an honest call at the walkthrough.
//   - PET URINE. Named in FAQ 4 because it is the single most searched carpet
//     problem and the most commonly over-promised. The answer is deliberately
//     hedged. Confirm whether TLB does sub-surface urine treatment or only
//     surface cleaning, and cut the claim if it is the latter.
//   - Drying time and pricing basis are bracketed. Both come up on the first
//     call.
//
// PHOTOGRAPHY. The hero is a family B cut-out keyed with
// scripts/key-cutout.mjs; prompts and the keying notes are in
// src/assets/home_cleaning/appliances/IMAGE-PROMPTS.md. Cards 2 and 3 are the
// two shared frames every page in this group uses.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/sections/SiteHeader.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/sections/Hero.astro';
import TrustBar from '../../components/sections/TrustBar.astro';
import Backdrop from '../../components/ui/Backdrop.astro';
import TextBlock from '../../components/sections/TextBlock.astro';
import PathwayCards from '../../components/sections/PathwayCards.astro';
import ServiceBlocks from '../../components/sections/ServiceBlocks.astro';
import TagCloud from '../../components/sections/TagCloud.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/sections/ComparisonTable.astro';
import GoogleReviewSlider from '../../components/sections/GoogleReviewSlider.astro';
import { googleBusinessProfileUrl, googleReviews } from '../../data/googleReviews';
import Faq from '../../components/sections/Faq.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/sections/CallToAction.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/sections/SiteFooter.astro';
import logoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-horizontal.png';
// §1 hero: family B cut-out, 1024x1024 PNG with a real alpha channel, so
// ratio 1/1 and contain-bottom. The figure faces LEFT, into the copy, because
// the image panel sits on the right.
// Cards 2 and 3 are shared by all six pages in this group — same subject,
// same file, per IMAGE-GUIDELINES §5.
// Pathway cards 2 and 3: real TLB photos (6 Oct 2026) already used on the
// homepage ("I need a hand at home") and the Airbnb page (card 1), copied
// here under carpet-page names and pre-cropped to the cards' 4:3.
import cardTeamImg from '../../assets/home_cleaning/appliances/carpet_and_rug/local-tlb-cleaner-wiping-a-kitchen-window-in-a-client-home.jpg';
import { whoIsInYourHomeCard } from '../../data/whoIsInYourHome';
import footerLogoImg from '../../assets/logo/tlb-logo-square.png';
import {
  primaryNav,
  headerNav,
  headerSecondaryCta,
  footerServiceLinks,
  footerContact,
  footerCopyright,
  quoteCta,
} from '../../data/navigation';
import { comparisonColumns, serviceComparisonRows } from '../../data/comparison';
import { footprintLocationGroups, footprintSubheading } from '../../data/locations';
import { trustBarCards } from '../../data/trust';
import { otherApplianceServices } from '../../data/appliance-services';
import { howItWorks, managedForYou, theLineBody } from '../../data/brand-lines';
import { localBusiness } from '../../data/business';
import { z } from 'astro/zod';
import { getPage } from '../../lib/cms';
import * as section from '../../lib/cms-schemas';
import { sized } from '../../lib/cms-schemas';

const OWN_HREF = '/house-cleaning/carpet-cleaning/';

// In `pageMeta`, on the title:
// Approved title and meta, pasted verbatim from the brief (workbook row 7)
// per its Rule 3. THE ROOT-CAUSE FIX: the live title split the mapped
// primary across "carpet AND RUG cleaning", and the scoring rules treat a
// split phrase as absent. This carries `carpet cleaning` 4,600/mo
// contiguously and picks up `carpet cleaning services` 800/mo plus the
// steam cluster at 1,900/mo (Keyword Mapping & Metadata, 15 Sep 2026).
//
// The hyphen construction and "Steam" sitting alone read a little abruptly.
// Approved, well inside the limit, and it does the keyword job, so it is
// pasted verbatim. Raising it would be a style preference, not a finding.
// In `pageMeta`, on the description:
// 144 characters. The live one was 166 and would have been truncated.
//
// WARNING: TWO PROMISES IN THIS META THE PAGE MUST KEEP.
//   - "Rugs and stairs included." Rugs were covered well; the word STAIRS
//     appeared nowhere on the live page. Landed in the hero lead and in
//     method stage three below. Fixed in copy.
//   - "steam or dry methods to suit your carpet." The page describes hot
//     water extraction as what TLB does, and names dry cleaning and
//     encapsulation only as other methods that exist. NOTHING SAYS TLB
//     OFFERS A DRY METHOD. That cannot be fixed in copy without an answer
//     from TLB. See the launch blockers in the file header.

// The primary CTA, defined once and repeated in four places per BFD 9.5: the
// hero button, pathway card 1, the button after the six stages and the
// closing block.
//
// This REMOVES a live contradiction rather than creating one. The page told
// the reader in its own words that "the honest answer is a fast quote rather
// than an instant one", and then put "Get an instant quote" on four buttons.
// BFD 13.2 agrees with the paragraph, not the buttons, and 3.3 is where
// booking online in a couple of minutes comes from.
const primaryCta = { label: 'Book your clean online' };

// In `business`, on `areaServed`:
// Residential pages claim the full service area, including QLD. Only the
// commercial pages are NSW-only, and that is a live open item over there.

// In `hero`, on `headingLines`:
// Brief section 4. `carpet cleaning` 4,600/mo is worth 15 points scored
// present or absent, and the region extension serves `carpet cleaning near
// me` 3,100/mo and `carpet cleaning services near me` 200/mo, together the
// second largest block of demand in the cluster.
//
// ON SAYING "CLEANING" TWICE: deliberate. "Carpet and rug cleaning" splits
// the target and "carpet cleaning and rugs" reads as though rugs are an
// afterthought. Saying it out gives both services their own noun and keeps
// the mapped phrase whole at the front. Rugs are not being dropped
// anywhere on this page; they move a few words to the right.
// In `hero`, on `lead`:
// Brief sections 5 and 6, in that order. The demoted H1 opens the lead, so
// it is still the first thing under the headline. Hero has no separate
// subheading slot; `headingLines` all render inside the one <h1>.
//
// Four added words honour the approved meta's stairs promise.
// In `hero`, on "A cleaner kneeling beside a bed to run a carpet extraction wand across a rug":
// Client-supplied image since 6 Oct 2026, replacing the transparent
// cut-out (which ran with `contain-bottom`; that file still serves the
// carpet cleaning guide). Default `cover` fit now. The supplied image is
// AI-edited (its book covers rendered as garbled text), so it is not
// described as an unedited photo anywhere. Retouched 6 Oct 2026 to read
// less generated: the bookcase is defocused so the covers are background
// blur, the colour is matched to the real photo of this same room, and
// phone-style grain is added. The file is a 0.9:1 crop, window to rug: the
// desktop panel is roughly square on these long-heading pages, and this
// shows the frame's full width there. `ratio` is the mobile fallback.

// §2 Definition. The answer-target block for the focus keyword. Paragraph two
// does the synonym work and, more usefully, draws the carpet/rug distinction
// that the rest of the page depends on.

// §4 Method. Six stages in the order they happen. The wool card is the one
// that matters most: it is the page's central claim and its biggest open
// question. See the file header.
//
// In `methodItems`, on "Traffic lanes, stairs and spots by hand":
// Brief section 14. The approved meta promises "Rugs and stairs included"
// and stairs appeared nowhere on the live page. This is the stage where
// they genuinely belong, and the added sentence is a real specific rather
// than a keyword insert.
// In `methodItems`, on the description of "Wool and natural fibres, differently":
// ⚠️ LAUNCH BLOCKER. Confirm TLB cleans wool at all — see the file
// header. If it refers these on, this card says so instead.
// In `methodItems`, on the description of "Groomed and dried":
// ⚠️ Bracket is real. Depends on equipment nobody has specified.

// §5 "Worth knowing". Same job as every sibling's version of this block: make
// the reader distrust the cheapest quote without making a claim about TLB.
// The lever here is that the cheap method looks identical on the day.

// NEW SECTION, brief section 18. End of lease carpet cleaning.
//
// Targets `end of lease carpet cleaning` 250/mo (Keyword Mapping & Metadata,
// 15 Sep 2026), captured at ZERO on the live page, which did not use the
// words bond, lease or inspection anywhere.
//
// WHY IT IS SHORT, and deliberately so: the site already has a dedicated
// /house-cleaning/end-of-lease-cleaning/ page with its own mapped cluster.
// This covers the carpet-specific slice, says the useful thing, and hands
// the reader across. Written any longer it would start competing with a
// stronger page for the same queries, which is the mistake this kind of
// addition usually makes.
//
// Placed immediately after "What a low carpet quote usually leaves out".

// The brief asks for this as anchor text on the heading or the last sentence.
// TextBlock renders plain paragraphs with no inline markup, so it lands as
// the block's own link instead. It is NAVIGATION to a sibling page, not a
// second primary CTA: the page's one CTA is `primaryCta` and it is repeated
// four times, per BFD 9.5.

const clusterServices = otherApplianceServices(OWN_HREF);

// In `comparisonTable`, on `rows`:
// Brief section 20, scorecard finding 7. The holiday-lets row comes off:
// the other seven rows all bear on a household booking a carpet clean, and
// this one is about a service the page does not sell. "Who cleans your
// home" IS correct here and stays, unlike on the two commercial pages in
// the earlier batch. See data/comparison.ts.

// In `brandedFaqItems`, on the answer to "Can you clean our wool rug?":
// ⚠️ Depends on the launch blocker in the file header. Written as the
// honest version of the answer either way.
// In `brandedFaqItems`, on "Is it worth paying someone, or should we just hire a machine?":
// NEW, brief section 17, added here as question 6.
//
// Targets `professional carpet cleaning` 1,000/mo (Keyword Mapping &
// Metadata, 15 Sep 2026), which the page captured only in passing. It
// made the professional case implicitly all the way through and never
// answered the question the searcher is actually asking. On the live
// SERP (16 Sep 2026) a direct local competitor leads with the DIY
// machine comparison, so this is a competitive gap as well as a
// coverage one.
//
// Answering it honestly, INCLUDING how to do it better yourself, is the
// BFD 2.3 move and costs almost nothing in bookings. Do not cut the last
// sentence: it is the part that makes the rest believable.

// §12 Non-branded FAQs.
//
// ⚠️ VERIFICATION PASS REQUIRED. These are checkable claims:
//   - Hot water extraction is the method most carpet manufacturers name in
//     their care instructions. Correct in substance; no interval is stated
//     because it varies by maker.
//   - Wool needs gentler pH and less moisture than synthetics. Correct and
//     uncontroversial.
//   - Pet urine penetrates to the backing and underlay. Correct, and the
//     reason the answer is hedged rather than promising removal.
//   - Dust mites: the answer deliberately makes NO health claim. Mite
//     allergen is a health topic and BFD 5.3 keeps this business out of it,
//     the same way the mould page does. Do not add one.
//
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on the answer to "Does carpet cleaning get rid of pet smells?":
// ⚠️ Deliberately hedged. See the launch blocker in the file header.
// In `nonBrandedFaqItems`, on the answer to "How much does carpet cleaning cost?":
// ⚠️ BRACKETED ON PURPOSE. Most searched question on the topic, and the
// page cannot answer it without a number from TLB. A wrong "from $X"
// is worse than no number, and the ACCC treats from-pricing as a claim.


// The page's default button: `primaryCta`'s label on the shared quote link.
// Used where the content file leaves a button empty (the hero and the closing
// block) and on the button after the six stages. Pathway card 1 carries the
// same label and link in the content file.
const primaryButton = { label: primaryCta.label, href: quoteCta.href };

// CONTENT lives in src/content/pages/house-cleaning/carpet-cleaning.yaml and
// is edited in Pages CMS ("Carpet cleaning", under House cleaning). This file
// owns the layout. The notes above explain why each section says what it
// says; they stay here because Pages CMS rewrites the YAML on save and would
// drop them.
const page = await getPage(
  'house-cleaning/carpet-cleaning',
  z.object({
    seo: section.seo,
    hero: section.hero,
    // Its background photo sits behind the trust bar and this block together
    // (the Backdrop below), so it cannot be left empty.
    definition: section.textBlock.extend({ backgroundImage: section.backgroundPhoto }),
    // The page's own cards. The "who is in my home" card after them is
    // shared, from Site settings.
    pathways: section.pathwayCards,
    method: section.iconGrid,
    worthKnowing: section.textBlock,
    endOfLease: section.textBlock,
    // Heading and lead only: the rows are the other appliance pages, from the
    // shared cross-link list.
    otherServices: section.sectionIntro,
    // The table's columns and rows are the shared comparison table.
    comparison: section.comparisonTable.omit({ columns: true, rows: true }),
    reviews: section.sectionHeading,
    // Subheading optional here: left empty, the band uses the shared
    // footprint line from Locations, as it always has.
    whereWeClean: section.tagCloud.extend({ subheading: section.optional(section.text) }),
    // Heading only: the paragraphs under it all come from Brand lines.
    brandLine: section.sectionHeading,
    faq: section.faq,
    nonBrandedFaq: section.faq,
    closingCta: section.callToAction,
  }),
);

const pageMeta = {
  ...page.seo,
  canonical: 'https://tlbcleaning.com.au/house-cleaning/carpet-cleaning/',
};

const business = localBusiness({
  description: pageMeta.description,
  // Residential pages claim the full service area, including QLD. Only the
  // commercial pages are NSW-only, and that is a live open item over there.
  areaServed: 'Northern Rivers NSW and Southern Gold Coast QLD',
  sameAs: googleBusinessProfileUrl ? [googleBusinessProfileUrl] : [],
});

const heroImage = page.hero.image && sized(page.hero.image, '1/1');

const ownCards = page.pathways.cards.map((card, i) => ({
  number: i + 1,
  ...card,
  image: sized(card.image, '4/3'),
}));
const pathwayCards = [
  ...ownCards,
  {
    ...whoIsInYourHomeCard(cardTeamImg, 'A local TLB cleaner wiping down the kitchen window in a client home'),
    number: ownCards.length + 1,
  },
];
---

<Base title={pageMeta.title} description={pageMeta.description} canonical={pageMeta.canonical} business={business}>
  <SiteHeader
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: logoImg }}
    primaryNav={primaryNav}
    serviceNav={headerNav}
    secondaryCta={headerSecondaryCta}
    cta={quoteCta}
  />

  <main id="main">
    <Hero
      variant="split-single-image"
      imagePosition="right"
      kicker={page.hero.kicker}
      headingLines={page.hero.headingLines}
      subheading={page.hero.subheading}
      lead={page.hero.lead}
      cta={page.hero.cta ?? primaryButton}
      image={heroImage}
    />

    <Backdrop image={page.definition.backgroundImage} tint="muted" opacity={90}>
      <TrustBar variant="card" cards={trustBarCards} />
      <TextBlock
        theme="muted"
        align="left"
        heading={page.definition.heading}
        body={page.definition.body}
        cta={page.definition.cta}
      />
    </Backdrop>

    <PathwayCards heading={page.pathways.heading} headingAccent={page.pathways.headingAccent} cards={pathwayCards} />

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="icon-grid"
      heading={page.method.heading}
      lead={page.method.lead}
      items={page.method.items}
      cta={page.method.cta ?? primaryButton}
    />

    <TextBlock
      theme="dark"
      align="left"
      heading={page.worthKnowing.heading}
      body={page.worthKnowing.body}
      cta={page.worthKnowing.cta}
      backgroundImage={page.worthKnowing.backgroundImage}
    />

    {/* Brief section 18. New H2. `light` between the dark "low quote" band
        above and the list block below, so the page keeps alternating rather
        than stacking two filled bands. */}
    <TextBlock
      theme="light"
      align="left"
      heading={page.endOfLease.heading}
      body={page.endOfLease.body}
      cta={page.endOfLease.cta}
      backgroundImage={page.endOfLease.backgroundImage}
    />

    {/* ⚠️ RESERVED SLOT: before and after slider (BeforeAfter.astro).
        Carpet is the best before/after subject on this site. NOT BUILT
        because the component's `src` is required by design and generated
        pairs are barred by IMAGE-GUIDELINES §7. It needs real photography:
        one traffic lane, tripod locked off, before and after, nothing moved
        between frames. Drop it in here. */}

    <ServiceBlocks
      variant="list"
      heading={page.otherServices.heading}
      lead={page.otherServices.lead}
      items={clusterServices.map((service) => ({
        icon: 'spray-bottle' as const,
        title: service.label,
        description: service.blurb,
        href: service.href,
      }))}
    />

    <ComparisonTable
      heading={page.comparison.heading}
      cornerLabel={page.comparison.cornerLabel}
      lead={page.comparison.lead}
      columns={comparisonColumns}
      rows={serviceComparisonRows()}
      footnote={page.comparison.footnote}
      cta={page.comparison.cta}
    />

    <GoogleReviewSlider heading={page.reviews.heading} reviews={googleReviews} profileUrl={googleBusinessProfileUrl} />

    <TagCloud
      heading={page.whereWeClean.heading}
      subheading={page.whereWeClean.subheading ?? footprintSubheading}
      tags={page.whereWeClean.tags}
      groups={footprintLocationGroups}
      note={page.whereWeClean.note}
    />

    {/* §1.3 The Line as a section heading, with §1.4 as its standfirst.
        The copy, and the reason this page gets `fast` rather than the other
        variant, both live in data/brand-lines.ts. Change it there, not here.

        `muted`, not `dark`: TagCloud above paints --color-brand and Faq below
        paints --color-surface, so Cream between them keeps the page
        alternating instead of stacking two dark bands.

        No CTA prop. §9.5 wants one primary CTA per page, repeated, and the
        closing CallToAction is directly under the FAQs. */}
    <TextBlock
      theme="muted"
      align="left"
      heading={page.brandLine.heading}
      body={[managedForYou.oneOff, ...theLineBody.residential, ...howItWorks.general]}
    />

    {/* Brief sections 24 and 25. The page carried two FAQ headings and the
        generic one made the split look like a build error. This block is
        about working with TLB, the next is about the service. The second
        rename also lands the mapped phrase contiguously in a heading, which
        is the 10-point H2 component the page only half scored.

        PROTECT non-branded question 4. The pet urine answer explains
        sub-surface contamination and says replacing the underlay is
        sometimes the only honest answer. It costs TLB a booking to say that,
        which is precisely why it is the most trustworthy paragraph on the
        page. Add to it if you must, never cut it. */}
    <Faq heading={page.faq.heading} lead={page.faq.lead} items={page.faq.items} />
    <Faq heading={page.nonBrandedFaq.heading} lead={page.nonBrandedFaq.lead} items={page.nonBrandedFaq.items} />

    <CallToAction
      variant="secondary"
      kicker={page.closingCta.kicker}
      heading={page.closingCta.heading}
      lead={page.closingCta.lead}
      cta={page.closingCta.cta ?? primaryButton}
    />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter
    logo={{ label: 'TLB Cleaning', src: footerLogoImg }}
    columns={[
      { title: 'Services', links: footerServiceLinks },
      { title: 'Locations', links: [{ label: 'View all locations', href: '/locations/' }] },
    ]}
    contact={footerContact}
    copyright={footerCopyright}
  />
</Base>
